DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin us for a discussion of the novel\,\nTranscri
 ption\nby Ben Lerner.\nBen Lerner is back with a lightning flash of a nove
 l that is at once a gripping emotional drama and a brilliant examination o
 f the devices\, digital and literary\, we use to store—or to erase—our
  memories.\nThe narrator is to conduct an interview with Thomas\, his nine
 ty-year-old mentor and the father of his friend\, Max\, but he drops his s
 martphone in the hotel sink. He arrives at Thomas’ house with no recordi
 ng device\, a fact he is mysteriously unable to confess.\nWhat unfolds fro
 m this dreamlike circumstance is both the unforgettable story of the trian
 gle formed by Thomas\, Max\, and the narrator\, and a brilliant meditation
  on those technologies that enrich or impoverish our connection to one ano
 ther\, that store or obliterate memory. Utterly contemporary\, Lerner comb
 ines trenchant insight with lyric mystery. Ultimately\, Transcription demo
 nstrates what only a work of fiction can record.\nJoin us on Monday\, Augu
 st 17th and Tuesday\, August 18th for a thrilling conversation. We hope to
  see you there.\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (or anot
 her beverage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversation with our brillian
 t moderator\, Lee Suksi.\nA $20 credit toward any book in the shop *\nGET 
 YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nA few details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n*
 $20 book credit is valid on the night of attendance only (non-refundable a
 nd non-transferable).\nWine is served on the night of the event (ID requir
 ed).\nTickets are non-refundable within 7 days of the event\; due to limit
 ed capacity and planning\, we’re not able to transfer tickets to future 
 book club sessions.
